          "unit_id": "starting_up",
          "title": "Above the Bookshop",
          "description": "Condensa la información como en un texto formal: participle clauses. Además, phrasal verbs de negocio y dónde va el objeto: set up, take on, turn down, come up with.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "starting_up_lesson",
              "title": "Participle clauses",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Above the bookshop",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Agent",
                        "text": "Built in 1890, the building has been completely renovated. Having been empty for six months, the office is available immediately."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "It's lovely. Looking out of this window, I can see the street where I got lost on my first Saturday in Bristol."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Next to the café, opposite the cinema. I gave you directions, remember?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "How could I forget?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Agent",
                        "text": "If signed today, the contract would allow you to move in on Monday."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Having seen six other offices, I'd say this is the best by far."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Agreed. Not being an expert in property, though, I'd like to read the contract carefully first."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Agent",
                        "text": "Of course. Taken as a whole, the terms are very reasonable."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I'll call you this afternoon, having read every word."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "So, what are we calling the company?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Inspired by the first person who welcomed me to Bristol… Green Door Design."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "After Mrs Green's front door? She'll be thrilled."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Agent",
                        "text": "I'll leave you two to talk. Congratulations, by the way."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "January, year four. Lucía and Daniel are standing in an empty office above a bookshop on Park Street, with an estate agent."
                  }
